# macOS
.DS_Store
/intelligence-eval

# Estate data dropped beside the scripts that consume it — scanner exports, SBOMs, sidecars.
# `scripts/` is where these land on a working machine, and one of them was committed by a
# `git add -A scripts` on 2026-09-22 (a 1264-row scan export with image names, PURLs and file
# paths). Ignored here so the next one cannot ride along; the real discipline is staging explicit
# paths, not trusting a guard.
#
# JSON is ignored for the same reason and it is the COMMON case, not an edge one: the scripts
# themselves name `scripts/oamp.json` as the default SBOM (release-smoke-test.sh, and the
# gf-upload-sbom.sh usage example), and that file has always been a local drop — a real customer
# SBOM, never committed. Sidecar reports and scanner output land here too.
#
# Nothing in `scripts/` is tracked as .csv or .json today, so this hides no existing file. If one
# ever genuinely belongs in the repo — a fixture, not estate data — `git add -f` it deliberately.
scripts/*.csv
scripts/*.json
scripts/*_SBOM_Files_*/
